    "title": "Lack of rain drops North Pond levels",
    "text": "The director of public works said the reservoir at North Pond is 36 inches below the spillway due to coastal communities in southern Rhode Island experiencing “abnormally dry” conditions.\nMike Gray told the town council at its Sept. 15 meeting the dryness was due to lack of rainfall. Thirty-six inches below the spillway means the reservoir is about 58 percent full. When the capacity hits 50 percent, or 42 inches below the spillway, restrictions will be enacted.\nThere currently are no restrictions on watering in the utility district. The mandatory summer ban on lawn irrigation ended Sept. 15.\nCustomers caught breaking these regulations typically are warned for a first offense. These warnings, however, can escalate. The town council, sitting as the board of water and sewer commissioners, has jurisdiction.",
